[90mbrigada runs coding tasks on the agent CLIs you are signed in to. A foreman[0m
[90m(an agent) turns your request into a plan of tasks; workers (other agents)[0m
[90mwrite the code in their own git worktrees; your check command tests it; and[0m
[90man agent of a different model family reviews it. Four short steps follow.[0m
[90mThe engine mirrors plan files (titles, task states, dependencies,[0m
[90mbranches, open questions, extra repositories) to the brigada/plans[0m
[90mbranch of your remote; turn that off with[0m
[90m`brigada project set plan_files=off`.[0m
[90mNothing is written or started until you confirm at the end.[0m

